## Phase 2 — Bronze Ingestion

> **Entry point:** [`POST /api/bronze/plans`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/routes/bronze.py#L60-L63) → [`bronze_service.create_plan()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L158-L182)

### 2.1 Plan Creation

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    A["Cleaned job outputs"] --> B["Detect source system\n(filename suffix regex)"]
    A --> C["Detect period\n(date columns → min/max month)"]
    B --> D["Build Candidates"]
    C --> D
    D --> E["Query existing bronze layer\n(tables + live ingestions)"]
    E --> F["planner.plan()\ndecide action per table"]
    F --> G["Plan with items\n(draft status)"]
```

**Step by step:**

| Step | Code | Logic |
|------|------|-------|
| Source system | [`naming.source_system_from_filename()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/naming.py#L46-L60) | Regex against the file name (e.g., `ARR_pc0515.xlsx` → `pc0515`) |
| Period | [`_detect_period()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L185-L193) → [`periods.detect()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/periods.py#L113-L132) | Priority: accounting date columns → transaction date columns → month-named sheets. Produces a `Period(start="2024-01", end="2024-06")` |
| Table name | [`naming.table_name()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/naming.py#L67-L80) | Convention: `ext_<source>_<sheet_slug>`, or `ext_<source>_data` if sheets are period-named or were appended |
| Planner | [`planner.plan()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/planner.py) | Compares each candidate's columns + period against the existing bronze registry |

### 2.2 Planner Decision Logic

The planner in [`planner.py`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/planner.py) produces one `PlanItem` per cleaned output. Decisions:

| Scenario | Action | Needs confirmation? |
|----------|--------|-------------------|
| Table name is new (not in registry) | `CREATE` | No |
| Same file hash already ingested | `SKIP` | No (reviewer can override) |
| Period overlaps an existing load | `REPLACE` | **Yes** — deletes old rows first |
| Same columns, same order | `APPEND` | No |
| Same columns, different order | `REORDER` | No |
| Columns added or removed | `EVOLVE` | **Yes** — adds missing columns as `text` |
| Completely different schema | `NEW_TABLE` | **Yes** — creates a separate table |

Schema comparison uses [`schema_compare.compare()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_bronze/schema_compare.py) → returns `IDENTICAL`, `REORDERED`, `EVOLVED`, or `DIFFERENT`.

### 2.3 Human Review (Edit the Plan)

The reviewer can:
- Change the **source system** or **period** of any file → [`update_file()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L230-L250)
- Change the **table name** or **action** of any item → [`update_item()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L253-L270)

Every edit triggers `_replan()` — the entire plan is rebuilt from scratch with the same inputs + the reviewer's overrides, so the plan shown is always the one that would run.

### 2.4 Approval & Execution

[`approve()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L280-L313):

1. **Staleness check** — replans once more; if the signature changed since review, rejects
2. **Blocker check** — every risky action (`replace`, `evolve`, `new_table`) must be explicitly confirmed
3. Launches `_run()` in a daemon thread

[`_execute()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/bronze_service.py#L372-L411) — **one database transaction for the entire plan**:

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    A["pg_advisory_xact_lock\n('ahi-bronze')"] --> B["For each item"]
    B --> C{"Action?"}
    C -->|skip| D["Audit row only"]
    C -->|create| E["CREATE TABLE ext_... (col text, ...)\n+ lineage columns"]
    C -->|append / reorder| F["INSERT via COPY"]
    C -->|evolve| G["ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN ...\nthen INSERT via COPY"]
    C -->|replace| H["DELETE old ingestion's rows\nthen INSERT via COPY"]
    E --> I["Row count check\n(loaded == cleaned)"]
    F --> I
    G --> I
    H --> I
    I --> J["Update bronze_table registry\n(columns, datatypes)"]
    J --> K["Audit row\n(ingestion table)"]
```

**Key details of `_load()`:**

- All data columns are stored as **`text`** — no typing in bronze
- 4 lineage columns are added: `_ingestion_id`, `_source_file`, `_source_sheet`, `_ingested_at`
- Data is written via `COPY FROM STDIN` (streaming, row by row from the Polars DataFrame)
- A post-load row count is verified against the cleaned table's height
- The `bronze_table` registry row is upserted with the merged column list + inferred datatypes

> **Output:** Bronze tables in PostgreSQL schema (`ext_bronze`), each with `text` columns + lineage. The `control.ingestion` audit table tracks every load.

