## Phase 3 — Silver Load

> **Entry point:** [`POST /api/silver/runs`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/routes/silver.py#L112-L114) → [`silver_service.create_run()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/silver_service.py#L259-L317)

### 3.1 Eligibility

[`eligible()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/silver_service.py#L122-L141) — queries bronze loads where `status = 'ingested' AND silver_status IS DISTINCT FROM 'succeeded'`. These are loads that reached bronze but haven't been successfully promoted to silver yet.

### 3.2 Run Creation (Column Matching)

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    A["Selected bronze loads\n(ingestion_ids)"] --> B["Group by bronze table"]
    B --> C["Read bronze columns + sample rows"]
    C --> D["Load Silver column catalog\n(silver_columns.csv)"]
    D --> E["Load approved mappings\n(column_mapping table)"]
    E --> F["5 independent matchers vote"]

    F --> G["saved — this table's approved mapping"]
    F --> H["exact — word-for-word match with Silver/DRT name"]
    F --> I["fuzzy — spelling distance (rapidfuzz)"]
    F --> J["semantic — word2vec cosine similarity"]
    F --> K["AI — LLM reads the column name + samples\n(Azure OpenAI or Gemini)"]

    G --> L["Pool votes into candidates\nRank by: own > support count > best score"]
    H --> L
    I --> L
    J --> L
    K --> L
    L --> M["Pre-select best candidate\nper bronze column"]
    M --> N["Dry-run transform\n(quality report)"]
```

The **Silver catalog** is defined in [`silver_columns.csv`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/config/silver_columns.csv):

| Silver column | DRT name | Type | Business key? |
|---------------|----------|------|---------------|
| `profit_center_name` | Profit Center Name | text | no |
| `profit_center_number` | Profit Center Number | text | yes |
| `insurance_company_name` | Insurance Company Name | text | yes |
| `producer_name` | Producer Name | text | no |
| `policy_number` | Policy Number | text | yes |
| `premium` | Premium | decimal | no |
| `commission` | Commission | decimal | no |
| `accounting_effective_date` | Accounting Effective Date | date | no |
| `policy_effective_date` | Policy Effective Date | date | no |
| `transaction_effective_date` | Transaction Effective Date | date | yes |
| `line_of_business` | Line of Business | text | no |

The matching logic lives in [`matching.suggest()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_silver/matching.py):

- Each method votes independently with a score (0–1)
- Votes for the same Silver column are pooled into a **candidate**
- Candidates are ranked: own approved mapping first → then by support count → then by highest weighted score
- The top candidate is pre-selected as the **recommendation**
- The reviewer sees all candidates with their method backing and can override any choice

### 3.3 Human Review (Edit Mappings)

For each bronze column, the reviewer can:
- Accept the recommendation
- Pick any other candidate
- Pick any Silver column (even one nobody voted for)
- Mark as **Ignored** (column is not loaded)

Each edit triggers [`_quality()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/silver_service.py#L324-L327) — a dry-run transform of the bronze rows using the current mapping, producing a live quality report showing invalid values, profit center lookup status, and unmapped Silver columns.

### 3.4 Approval & Execution

[`approve()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/silver_service.py#L395-L421):

1. Checks every column is either mapped or ignored
2. Validates that bronze tables and Silver catalog haven't changed since review
3. Launches `_run()` in a daemon thread

[`_execute()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/api/services/silver_service.py#L492-L577) — **one database transaction**:

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    A["pg_advisory_xact_lock\n('ahi-silver')"] --> B["Staleness re-check"]
    B --> C["Ensure tables exist\n(detail, summary, column_mapping)"]
    C --> D["Step 1: Save approved mapping\nINSERT INTO column_mapping"]
    D --> E["Step 2: Remove superseded loads\nDELETE FROM detail\nWHERE _ingestion_id = superseded"]
    E --> F["Step 3: For each table"]
    F --> G["Read bronze rows\n(all text + lineage)"]
    G --> H["transform.transform()"]
    H --> I["Type cast per Silver column\n(text→date, text→decimal)"]
    H --> J["Profit center resolution\n(LOTL lookup)"]
    H --> K["Compute hashes\n(business_key_hash, row_hash)"]
    I --> L["COPY INTO detail"]
    J --> L
    K --> L
    L --> M["Row count verification"]
    M --> N["Mark ingestion.silver_status = 'succeeded'"]
    N --> O["Step 4: Rebuild summary\n(GROUP BY pc_id, month)"]
    O --> P["Audit row in silver_run table"]
```

### 3.5 The Transform ([`transform.transform()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_silver/transform.py#L20-L82))

This is the core Bronze → Silver conversion:

1. **Column selection** — for each Silver catalog column, find the mapped bronze column (or NULL if unmapped)
2. **Type casting** ([`cleanse.by_type()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_silver/cleanse.py)) — cast `text` → `date`, `text` → `numeric(18,2)`, or keep as `text`, counting failures
3. **Profit center resolution** ([`profit_center.resolve()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_silver/profit_center.py)) — looks up the LOTL table to normalize profit center names/numbers; produces a status per row (`exact_match`, `name_only`, `number_only`, `lotl_unavailable`, etc.)
4. **Hashing** ([`hashing.digest()`](file:///c:/Exavalu_internal_projects/excel_cleaner_proj/Dirty_excel_cleaner/backend/src/ahi_silver/hashing.py)):
   - `business_key_hash` — SHA-256 of the business-key columns (policy number, profit center number, etc.)
   - `row_hash` — SHA-256 of all Silver columns
5. **Extra columns** added: `pc_id`, `pc_lookup_status`, `business_key_hash`, `row_hash`
6. **Lineage preserved**: `_bronze_table`, `_ingestion_id`, `_source_file`, `_source_sheet`, `_silver_run_id`, `_loaded_at`

### 3.6 Silver Schema

The `detail` table contains:

| Column group | Columns | Source |
|-------------|---------|--------|
| Silver catalog | `profit_center_name`, `profit_center_number`, `insurance_company_name`, `producer_name`, `policy_number`, `premium`, `commission`, `accounting_effective_date`, `policy_effective_date`, `transaction_effective_date`, `line_of_business` | Mapped from bronze via approved mapping |
| Profit center | `pc_id`, `pc_lookup_status` | LOTL lookup |
| Hashes | `business_key_hash`, `row_hash` | Computed |
| Lineage | `_bronze_table`, `_ingestion_id`, `_source_file`, `_source_sheet`, `_silver_run_id`, `_loaded_at` | Carried from bronze |

The `summary` table is rebuilt per profit center:
- `GROUP BY pc_id, profit_center_number, profit_center_name, date_trunc('month', accounting_effective_date)`
- Aggregates: `count(*)`, `sum(premium)`

