## End-to-End Data Lineage

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Excel cell\n(row 15, col B,\nSheet 'Jan')"] --> B["Cleaned row\n(trace: header row 3,\njunk rows dropped)"]
    B --> C["CSV output\n(job_id/file.csv)"]
    C --> D["Bronze row\n(_ingestion_id,\n_source_file='Report.xlsx',\n_source_sheet='Jan')"]
    D --> E["Silver detail row\n(_bronze_table='ext_pc0515_arr',\n_ingestion_id,\n_silver_run_id,\n_source_file,\n_source_sheet)"]
```

Every row in Silver can be traced back to:
1. Which Silver run loaded it (`_silver_run_id`)
2. Which bronze ingestion it came from (`_ingestion_id`)
3. Which bronze table it was in (`_bronze_table`)
4. Which original Excel file it came from (`_source_file`)
5. Which sheet within that file (`_source_sheet`)
6. The cleaning job's audit report has the exact row numbers, header decisions, and which rows were dropped and why

